Pouch kill(pid, 0) and getppid over the native probe and SYS_GETPPID (B-3b, vote 6).

kill(pid, 0) answered EINVAL: signal 0 maps to no note. It is now SYS_postnote
with an empty name, the kernel's probe (operator vote 2026-10-14 #6), which
asks the post's gate and posts nothing: 0 for the caller itself, pid 0 and a
child (dead but unreaped included), ESRCH for a missing pid, and the gate's
EACCES spelled EPERM, as kill() spells it for every other signal.

getppid() returned the 0xFFFF sentinel's -ENOSYS as the parent's pid (-38).
It is now native SYS_GETPPID (132), as getpid is native 72; it never fails.

